{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8053","id":5228359830,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABN6Jwlg","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8053","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8053.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8053.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8053","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8053/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8053/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8053/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/fafcc12754c4ff92629bfd21d5fd951097374bd7","number":8053,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(pm-dispatch): read/status endpoints for tasks and sessions","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes the pm-dispatch interface gaps filed in #5555 (fleet epic #5412 step 4 follow-on).\n\n## Gap 1 — read/status endpoints (implemented)\n- `GET /v1/tasks/:id` — authenticated (same OIDC/bearer auth as the POST routes, via the existing `authenticate()`). Returns the task row status surface: status, worker_id, lane_id, progress, result, attempts/lease/timestamps, plus the packet repo/kind. The packet body and payload are NOT returned — a status surface, not a packet dump — and a task whose packet names a repo is gated by `assertCallerRepo` for that repo. Unknown id → 404, non-numeric id → 400, queue unconfigured → 502. Backed by the existing `QueueClient.getTask`.\n- `GET /v1/sessions/:id` — authenticated; proxies the OpenCode server via a new `OpenCodeClient.getSession` (404 → null → route 404; other OpenCode failures stay 502, so gone is never conflated with unknown). Returns `{session_id, title, directory, time}`.\n\n## Gap 2 — token vault home (docs)\nThe value already lives in Bitwarden as `pm-dispatch.api-token`; the durable gap was documentation. README Auth section and the install.sh header now name that vault home alongside `~/secrets/dispatch.env`, so a rotation updates both places.\n\n## Tests\n- New: view-shaping unit tests (task/session), route auth/wiring tests (401 unauthenticated, 400 bad id, 502 queue-unconfigured) in test/server.test.ts; getSession 200/404/500 tests in test/opencode.test.ts.\n- Full dispatch suite: 168 pass / 0 fail.\n- Typecheck: no errors in touched files (4 pre-existing errors in test/auth.test.ts and test/queue.test.ts under the locally installed latest @types/bun; without node_modules tsc fails earlier with the pre-existing TS2688 on clean main too).\n\nQueue task 14286 (lane code-m, direct execution lane); worked in fallback mode after the primary store rejected the checkpoint for this task (mid-shift fallback per runbook §0b).\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added authenticated endpoints to check task and session status. Task responses include selected status and metadata without exposing packet contents; access follows repository permissions.\n  * Session status responses provide a concise view of session details, including its directory. Missing sessions and service errors return appropriate responses.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Documented the task and session status endpoints, their access rules, and common error responses.\n  * Clarified where the dispatch API token is stored and what must be updated during rotation.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T17:40:34Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T07:06:56Z","closed_at":"2026-11-11T07:06:54Z","merged_at":"2026-11-11T07:06:54Z","merge_commit_sha":"d555a807cb8cb27aeaf1427a525520f3f6c9b97f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549","members_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/members{/member}","name":"codeowners","description":"Team Discussions: developing-today/code","permission":"pull","privacy":"closed","notification_setting":"notifications_enabled","html_url":"https://github.com/orgs/developing-today/teams/codeowners","repositories_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/repos","slug":"codeowners","type":"organization","organization_id":26439447,"parent":null}],"head":{"label":"developing-today:queue/14286-5555-dispatch-status","ref":"queue/14286-5555-dispatch-status","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","g